{"name":"Mulch","hex":"#4e4240","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"mulch","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["Any material used to cover the top layer of soil to protect, insulate, or decorate it, or to discourage weeds or retain moisture."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To apply mulch.","To turn into mulch."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/mulch"}],"entries":[{"title":"Mulch","blocks":[{"text":"A mulch is a layer of material applied to the surface of soil. Reasons for applying mulch include conservation of soil moisture, improving fertility and health of the soil, reducing weed growth, and enhancing the visual appeal of the area."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/58/Rindenmulch016.JPG/330px-Rindenmulch016.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Mulch","wikidata":"Q549563"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/98/Rubber_mulch.jpg/500px-Rubber_mulch.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/98/Rubber_mulch.jpg/1280px-Rubber_mulch.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/98/Rubber_mulch.jpg/500px-Rubber_mulch.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Rubber mulch nuggets in a playground. The white fibers are nylon cords, which are present in the tires from which the mulch is made.","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ARubber_mulch.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f1/Mulch.jpg/330px-Mulch.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f1/Mulch.jpg/330px-Mulch.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content